meta {
  name: Sync Branch Lab Panels
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/branch-lab-panels/sync
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "listId": "{{branchLabPanelListId}}"
  }
}

tests {
  test("201/200", function () {
    expect([200, 201]).to.include(res.getStatus());
  });
  test("reports created/updated/deleted/failed", function () {
    const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
    expect(data).to.have.property("created");
    expect(data).to.have.property("updated");
    expect(data).to.have.property("deleted");
    expect(data).to.have.property("failed");
  });
}

docs {
  **Reconcile** a branch's Lab Panel List against its Branch Master Data so the
  list is an accurate reflection of it, scoped to one pricing list. Send `{}` for a
  full reconcile, or add `"branchLabPanelIds": ["<id>", ...]` to restrict
  update/delete to a subset (a subset run never adds).

  `listId` (optional) targets a specific `BranchLabPanelList` — must belong to the
  caller's branch (404 `BRANCH_LAB_PANEL_LIST_NOT_FOUND` otherwise). Omit it to
  sync the branch's default **Walk-in** panel list, always ensured first. Member
  tests are always rebuilt into the Walk-in **test** list, same as import.

  **Reconcile semantics** (Master Data is the source of truth):
  - **UPDATE** — an existing imported original is re-snapshotted and its member
    composition (`BranchLabPanelTest`) rebuilt from the source.
  - **DELETE** — an imported original whose source no longer exists in Master Data
    is soft-deleted (joins retired; a sibling promoted to default if needed).

  Sync does **not** ADD — adding is "Import from Master Data" (so `created` is
  always 0). User duplicates are never touched. Writes commit in batches and a
  failing batch is counted and skipped → `{ created, updated, deleted, failed }`.

  This is the synchronous endpoint (also the FE's fallback). For live progress use
  the background job: `POST /branch-lab-panels/sync/jobs` (see "Start Sync Job").
}
